-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",59,{
[1857]="700579EF\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tMithrandir is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Cúfaron is hopeful that some of Merry and Pippin's chatter may have had a kernel of truth, and he wants you to find the wizard of whose fireworks they spoke.\n2\tFind Gandalf's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tMithrandir told you he has assembled quite a stock of fireworks during the days following the end of the war, and he keeps them in a crate in his quarters in the High Guest-house, located in the Seventh Circle.\n3\tTake fireworks out of the crate\tThe crate of fireworks is in Mithrandir's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle. Mithrandir did not specify which of the fireworks to bring to him. Better take everything out of the crate, just to be safe!\n4\tTake more fireworks out of the crate\tThe crate of fireworks is in Mithrandir's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle. Mithrandir did not specify which of the fireworks to bring to him. Better take everything out of the crate, just to be safe!\n5\tTake some more fireworks out of the crate\tThe crate of fireworks is in Mithrandir's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle. Mithrandir did not specify which of the fireworks to bring to him. Better take everything out of the crate, just to be safe!\n6\tTake even more fireworks out of the crate\tThe crate of fireworks is in Mithrandir's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle. Mithrandir did not specify which of the fireworks to bring to him. Better take everything out of the crate, just to be safe!\n7\tWhy stop now? Take additional fireworks out of the crate\tThe crate of fireworks is in Mithrandir's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle. Mithrandir did not specify which of the fireworks to bring to him. Better take everything out of the crate, just to be safe!\n8\tHow many could there be? Take even more fireworks from the crate\tThe crate of fireworks is in Mithrandir's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle. Mithrandir did not specify which of the fireworks to bring to him. Better take everything out of the crate, just to be safe!\n9\tThere couldn't possibly be more, could there? Take more fireworks from the crate\tThe crate of fireworks is in Mithrandir's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle. Mithrandir did not specify which of the fireworks to bring to him. Better take everything out of the crate, just to be safe!\n10\tBring the impressive collection of fireworks to Mithrandir in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tMithrandir is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You have retrieved a truly impressive amount of fireworks from Mithrandir's quarters, and should now bring them to the Wizard.\n",
[1858]="70000414\n1\tSpeak to Constable Underhill\tThe Blackwolds' old hideout is found south of the Combe guard-house, near Staddle Falls at the north-east end of Staddle pond. Constable Underhill has decided that it is probably a good idea to take a look in the Blackwolds' old hideout, to make sure they aren't mustering there again. He has asked, however, that you accompany him.\n2\tTalk to Constable Underhill\tSpeak to Constable Underhill. You infiltrated the Blackwolds' hideout and defeated several of them, at the request of Constable Underhill.\n",
[1859]="70061BCD\n1\tVisit Lhan Garan on the eastern edge of the Wadewater and learn if there was any sign of Tegwyn\tThe Dunlending village of Lhan Garan is north-east of Mossward, on the eastern side of the Wadewater. It would be a good place to start looking for Tegwyn.\n2\tTalk to Meneldir at Lhan Garan\tMeneldir has come to Lhan Garan on the Wadewater's edge.\n3\tDefeat avanc in the Wadewater (total: 6)\tAvanc in the Wadewater would be a real danger to Tegwyn. Defeating any of them you encounter can only help in your rescue efforts.\n4\tTalk to Meneldir in the middle of the Wadewater, west of Fangsettle\tMeneldir is in the middle of the Wadewater, west of Fangsettle.\n5\tListen for Tegwyn\tMeneldir asked you to listen for Tegwyn.\n6\tTalk to Meneldir in the Wadewater, west of Fangsettle\tMeneldir is in the middle of the Wadewater, west of Fangsettle.\n7\tSearch for Tegwyn further to the west in the Wadewater\tMeneldir suggested you continue the search for Tegwyn further to the west.\n8\tExamine the abandoned wooden sword\tYou found a worn wooden sword abandoned in the mud of the Wadewater.\n9\tTalk to Meneldir by the abandoned wooden sword in the Wadewater\tMeneldir has joined you in the Wadewater by an abandoned wooden sword.\n10\tListen for Tegwyn\tMeneldir asked you to listen for Tegwyn.\n11\tSearch for Tegwyn to the north-west in the Wadewater\tYou heard a faint voice calling for you to the north-west in the Wadewater. Is it Tegwyn?\n12\tTalk to Tegwyn in the north-western reaches of the Wadewater\tYou found Tegwyn in the Wadewater, safe and sound.\n",
[1860]="7003FDAF\n1\tJourney to the Dark Door, the entrance to the Paths of the Dead\tThe Dark Door is south-east of the camp at Dunharrow. Éowyn has charged you with travelling the Paths of the Dead and coming by that way into Gondor, where she asks that you protect the people of Gondor from the threat posed by the Ruthless Dead.\n2\tJourney through the Paths of the Dead beneath the Dwimorberg\tBuildings built by those who are Dead can be found beneath the Haunted Mountain, Dwimorberg. Éowyn has charged you with travelling the Paths of the Dead and coming by that way into Gondor, where she asks that you protect the people of Gondor from the threat posed by the Ruthless Dead.\n3\tCome safely through the Paths of the Dead to the Blackroot Vale\tThe Paths of the Dead lead beneath the Haunted Mountain, Dwimorberg, to the Blackroot Vale. Éowyn has charged you with travelling the Paths of the Dead and coming by that way into Gondor, where she asks that you protect the people of Gondor from the threat posed by the Ruthless Dead.\n4\tFind the hilltop settlement of Morlad, in the Blackroot Vale\tThe town of Morlad is on a hill on the western side of the Blackroot Vale. Éowyn has charged you with protecting the people of Gondor from any threat posed by the Ruthless Dead.\n5\tTalk to Celegdal at the entrance to Morlad\tA man has called for your attention at the entrance to Morlad, in the Blackroot Vale.\n6\tDefeat frenzied or maddened creatures throughout the Blackroot Vale (total: 10)\tCelegdal has asked you to defeat frenzied or maddened creatures throughout the Blackroot Vale, especially near the town of Morlad, including any creatures that might be susceptible.\n7\tTalk to Celegdal at the entrance to Morlad\tCelegdal is at the entrance to Morlad, in the Blackroot Vale. You have defeated frenzied creatures in the Vale and should now return to Celegdal.\n",
[1861]="7003FDB0\n1\tJourney to the summit of the Hill of Erech, east of Morlad\tThe Hill of Erech is east of Morlad, in the Blackroot Vale. Celegdal believes that a great evil came out of the mountains and went to the Hill of Erech, and wants you to see if it is true.\n2\tThe earth atop the Hill of Erech has been disturbed, and bears investigation.\t\n3\tYou have been seen against the sky atop the Hill of Erech!\tSomeone has seen you, silhouetted against the sky atop the Hill of Erech!\n4\tDescend the hill and find the man who called out to you\tSomeone saw you while you searched the summit of Erech, and called out to you. You should descend the hill and see if this person is a friend.\n",
[1862]="7000017B\n1\tTalk to Strider\tStrider is in his room at The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree, which is found by taking a left down the hall out of the common room until you can only bear right. The room is at the end of the hall to the right of the stairs. You should return to Strider and tell him what you learned about the Blackwolds and the Pale Dwarf.\n",
[1863]="70061BCE\n1\tTalk to Meneldir in the north-western Wadewater\tMeneldir stands in the north-west Wadewater, considering the words of Tegwyn.\n2\tFind Echad Terthas, the camp of Meneldir's kinsman Duindil, to the east of the Wadewater\tDuindil, a Ranger at Echad Terthas, may know about the Uruks marching within Caras Gelebren. Echad Terthas is located to the east of the Wadewater.\n3\tTalk to Duindil at Echad Terthas\tDuindil oversees the work at the camp of Echad Terthas, within view of the old Elf-city.\n4\tClimb the sloping path to the south-east of Echad Terthas\tDuindil guided you to spy upon the Uruks that occupy Caras Gelebren, suggesting that you climb the sloping path to the south-east of Echad Terthas.\n5\tExamine one of the Uruk corpses\tTwo Uruk corpses lie in the grass outside Caras Gelebren.\n6\tExamine the other Uruk corpse\tTwo Uruk corpses lie in the grass outside Caras Gelebren.\n7\tTalk to Bregoleth up the slope to the south\tAn Elf up the slope to the south has called for your attention. Did she slay these Uruks?\n",
[1864]="700579F2\n1\tFind Gimli in the Splintered Shield, located in the Second Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tGimli is in the Splintered Shield, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n2\tTalk to Gimli in the Splintered Shield\tGimli is in the Splintered Shield, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You have awoken Gimli from the drink-induced slumber of his creative process. Perhaps you should ask him about his success coming up with the right vows for the Great Wedding.\n3\tWake Drafli Broadshield in the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tDrafli Broadshield is in the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Drafli Broadshield has been working with Gimli to determine the proper vows for the Great Wedding. You should wake him up so you can hear the results.\n4\tTalk to Drafli in the Splintered Shield\tDrafli Broadshield is in the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n5\tTalk to the proprietor of the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tDegilion, the proprietor of the Splintered Shield, is always behind the bar. Drafli and Gimli are in agreement: the ale of the Splintered Shield should flow without limit at the feast that will follow the Great Wedding. Now it is up to you to make the arrangements with the proprietor of the tavern.\n6\tTalk to Gimli in the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tGimli is in the Splintered Shield, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n7\tGather up the messy papers (total: 5)\tGimli and Drafli's attempts to come up with the perfect vows for the Great Wedding are spread out on the table in front of the dwarves.\n8\tGive the bundle of papers to Gimli in the Splintered Shield\tGimli is in the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n",
[1865]="7003FDC7\n1\tTravel south-east through Tarlang's Neck into Lamedon\tRovalang has asked you to travel south-east through Tarlang's Neck, and to help any people of Gondor who may have run afoul of the Dead in their passage.\n2\tTalk to Bandron by his cart in Tarlang's Neck\tA waggon has come to an early stop in Tarlang's Neck, and its driver could use your assistance.\n3\tFind Nethadan somewhere south of Tarlang's Neck\tNethadan went to the town of Dínadab in Lamedon, south-east of Tarlang's Neck, to recover supplies to fix his father's broken waggon, but he never returned. Bandron asked for you to find him.\n4\tCollect barrel of nails by Nethadan\tNethadan has asked you to bring one of the barrels near him back to his father Bandron, in Tarlang's Neck.\n5\tBring the barrel of nails to Bandron by his cart in Tarlang's Neck\tBandron is by his broken cart in Tarlang's Neck, between Lamedon and Blackroot Vale. You have picked up a barrel of nails from Nethadan and he asked you to bring it to his father so he can repair the cart.\n6\tTalk to Galengam outside his shop in Calembel\tGalengam is outside his shop in Calembel, south-east of Tarlang's Neck. Bandron has asked you to speak to his employer in the town of Calembel and explain some of the reasons for the delay.\n",
[1866]="700579F3\n1\tAsk Degilion, proprietor of the Splintered Shield, about the scrawled threat\030Question a man of Gondor about the threat\030Question a woman of Gondor about the threat\tSomeone in the Splintered Shield, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer), may have seen something. Someone in the Splintered Shield placed that note on the table while Gimli and Drafli were preoccupied with their ales. But who could have done this, and why would they risk notice by the dwarves or their powerful friends?\n2\tTalk to Gimli in the Splintered Shield\tGimli is in the Splintered Shield, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n3\tShow the wrinkled note to Mithrandir in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tMithrandir is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Gimli wants you to show the scrawled threat to Mithrandir and get a Wizard's advice.\n4\tTalk to King Elessar in the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tKing Elessar is in the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n",
[1867]="70061BCF\n1\tDefeat Uruks within Caras Gelebren ([see journal]/10)\tUruks stalk the lanes of Caras Gelebren. Bregoleth asked you to defeat the Uruks that now prowl within Caras Gelebren.\n2\tDefeat Uruks within Caras Gelebren (9/10)\tUruks stalk the lanes of Caras Gelebren. Bregoleth asked you to defeat the Uruks that now prowl within Caras Gelebren.\n3\tRead the Uruk report you collected\tYou took a crumpled parchment from the body of an Uruk that stalked the lanes of Caras Gelebren. You should read the Uruk report and learn what you can of the creatures' purpose in Swanfleet.\n4\tBring the Uruk report to Bregoleth on the slope north-west of Caras Gelebren\tBregoleth is hunting Uruks north-west of Caras Gelebren. You should show Bregoleth the Uruk report you found on one of the creatures prowling within Caras Gelebren.\n",
[1868]="7000017C\n1\tTalk to Lenglinn\tLenglinn's camp sits on a rise north of the Buckland Gate, along the Great East Road, west of Bree. Strider has asked that you speak with Lenglinn, another Ranger, and learn if he has seen any other Nazgûl passing out of the Shire.\n",
[1869]="70061BD0\n1\tCollect an artifact from the centre of Caras Gelebren\030Collect an artifact from south-west Caras Gelebren\030Collect an artifact from south-east Caras Gelebren\030Examine the half-buried statue in the centre of Caras Gelebren\030Examine the damaged pillar in south-west Caras Gelebren\030Examine the fallen lamp in south-east Caras Gelebren\tBregoleth asked you to search Caras Gelebren for artifacts that might reveal Saruman's purpose in sending Uruks to Swanfleet.\n2\tBring the artifacts you collected to Bregoleth north-west of Caras Gelebren\tBregoleth is waiting on the descending slope north-west of Caras Gelebren for you to return with the artifacts you gathered.\n",
[1870]="70000205\n1\tDefeat crebain (total: 4)\tThe crebain have taken roost south-west, just beyond his camp. Lenglinn told you that crebain followed in the wake of the Nazgûl and have taken roost outside his camp. He is sure the birds are the Enemy's spies and will report on movements in the west. He has asked you to dispose of them to prevent them from doing harm.\n2\tTalk to Lenglinn\tLenglinn's camp is to the north-east of the crebain roost. With the crebain dead, the Enemy has fewer eyes watching Buckland and the Shire. Speak again with Lenglinn and learn what else he would have you do.\n",
[1871]="700579F4\n1\tTalk to Húrin the Tall at the gates to Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tHúrin the Tall, Warden of the Keys, is waiting for you to come down to the gates of the city so you may welcome the party from Rivendell.\n2\tWelcome the party from Rivendell outside the gates of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tThe party from Rivendell has been spotted to the north of Minas Tirith (Midsummer), and it is King Elessar's wish that you should greet them.\n3\tTalk to Elrohir\030Talk to Elladan\tYour friends among the travelling party wish to greet you after their long journey.\n4\tTalk to Glorfindel\030Talk to Erestor\tYour friends among the travelling party wish to greet you after their long journey.\n5\tTalk to Galadriel\030Talk to Celeborn\tYour friends among the travelling party wish to greet you after their long journey.\n6\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond smiles at you, his eyebrows raised with unexpected mirth. Even so, you know he feels a deep sorrow that his daughter will no longer accompany him to the Undying Lands.\n7\tTalk to Arwen Undómiel outside the city\tArwen Undómiel, Evenstar of her people, has come to Gondor. She wishes to speak with you.\n",
[1872]="7003FDC8\n1\tTalk to a Cemenduril farmer in the fields\030Collect Corsair weapons (total: 6)\030Retrieve harvested Cemenduril bundles (total: 3)\tGalengam's farmers can be found west of Calembel, working the flower fields. A wealthy merchant has asked you to protect the farmers that grow his Cemenduril crop from the attacks of any raiders that threaten.\n2\tBring Cemenduril bundles and Corsair weapons to Galengam\tGalengam is outside his shop in Calembel. You have protected Galengam's farmers and collected a number of weapons wielded by the Corsair raiders. The merchant will be interested to hear how you have assisted his interests.\n",
[1873]="700579FA\n1\tTalk to King Elessar outside the city\tKing Elessar has emerged from the city, eager to greet his bride, but first he has some words for you.\n2\tTalk to King Elessar outside the city and experience 'A Wedding at Midsummer'\tThe time of the wedding has arrived!\n3\tTalk to Rodwen outside the feast-hall of Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tRodwen is pleased at how well the ceremony was conducted, and now she wishes to speak with you outside the feast-hall of Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n",
[1874]="7003FDD3\n1\tFind the overlook west of Calembel, in Belfalas, that provides a good view of Edhellond\tAn overlook of the refuge of Edhellond, west of Calembel in Belfalas, would be a good place to begin your stand against the Corsair raiders. Galengam has sent you to Edhellond to deal with some of the Corsair raiders.\n2\tTalk to Lathlorn on the overlook near Edhellond\tLathlorn is surveying the situation at Edhellond, from an overlook that provides a good view of the refuge.\n3\tExplore the tallest tower at Edhellond\030Explore the southern court of Edhellond\030Explore the north-west dock at Edhellond\030Defeat Corsair raiders in Edhellond (total: 8)\030Collect relics in Edhellond (total: 6)\tLathlorn has asked you to explore the abandoned refuge of Edhellond, defeating Corsair raiders and collecting any relics of historical interest.\n4\tLathlorn is on an overlook with a good view of the Corsair landing at Edhellond. You have defeated Corsair raiders throughout Edhellond and collected a number of forgotten relics, and should bring them now to Lathlorn.\t\n",
[1875]="7000017D\n1\tInvestigate Crickhollow\tBaggins' home is at Crickhollow, almost due south-east of the Buckland Gate, south of Lenglinn's camp. In order to determine the movements of the Nazgûl, Lenglinn has asked you to investigate the home of a hobbit named Baggins.\n2\tTalk to Lenglinn\tLenglinn's camp is north of the Buckland Gate, north-west of Crickhollow. When you spoke to Fredegar Bolger, he told you that the Black Riders had not caught him and so learned nothing from him, but he let slip to you something about a Ring belonging to the Enemy. As Fredegar was speaking, crebain flew out of the sky and attacked him, and though you defeated the crebain, two retreated into the Old Forest. You should bring this news to Lenglinn.\n3\tTalk to Strider\tStrider is in his room at The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree, which is found by taking a left down the hall out of the common room until you can only bear right. The room is at the end of the hall to the right of the stairs. Lenglinn asked you to seek Strider's counsel on how to find the crebain that had overheard Fredegar Bolger's words and escaped into the Old Forest. He fears that if the Enemy learns that this Ring they seek is no longer in the Shire, all may be lost.\n",
[1876]="70061BD1\n1\tTalk to Bregoleth and hear of the years she spent in Eregion, long ago\tBregoleth has agreed to speak of the years she lived in Eregion, though the memories of that time are painful for her.\n2\tTalk to Bregoleth on the slope north-west of Caras Gelebren\tBregoleth desires to conclude her sad tale.\n3\tTalk to Meneldir on the slope north-west of Caras Gelebren\tThe Ranger Meneldir has arrived. He glances questioningly at Bregoleth.\n",
[1877]="7003FDDA\n1\tFind the entrance to the Cave of the Avorrim, overlooking the sea\tThe Cave of the Avorrim is located in a cliff-wall overlooking the sea, on the road to Dol Amroth. Lathlorn described it in this way: 'If you follow the road south-west on the way to Dol Amroth, you will come to a rocky cleft in the ground to your right. Follow it down to a cliff-side path over the water, and you will come to the entrance.'\n2\tFind Dorthaneth within the Cave of the Avorrim\tDorthaneth is within the Cave of the Avorrim, in Belfalas.\n3\tTalk to Dorthaneth in the Cave of the Avorrim\tDorthaneth is within the Cave of the Avorrim, in Belfalas. Lathlorn has sent you to speak with Dorthaneth, the leader of the Avorrim.\n4\tTalk to Galdor in the Cave of the Avorrim\tGaldor is in the Cave of the Avorrim, in Belfalas.\n5\tTalk to Dorthaneth in the Cave of the Avorrim\tDorthaneth is in the Cave of the Avorrim. Galdor, an emissary from Círdan the Shipright at Mithlond, has overheard the speech of the Corsair raiders, and is worried about the loyalty they display for their leaders.\n",
[1878]="7000013A\n1\tTalk to Tom Bombadil\tTom Bombadil's house is at the far eastern end of the River Withywindle in the Old Forest. Strider told you to seek out someone named Tom Bombadil and ask for his aid finding the crebain who flew into the Old Forest.\n",
[1879]="70061BD3\n1\tTalk to Bregoleth on the slope north-west of Caras Gelebren\tBregoleth is north-west of Caras Gelebren, hopeful that the purpose of the Uruks in Swanfleet can be hindered.\n2\tUruk tracks signifying the locations of Uruk war-leaders can be found at three different places in Western Eregion. Meneldir asked you to investigate Uruk tracks within Swanfleet and defeat one of the Uruk war-leaders responsible.\t\n3\tTalk to Meneldir at Idhobel\tIdhobel is located in Western Eregion, along the road that runs north to Tham Celechir. Meneldir and Bregoleth agreed to meet with you at Idhobel after each of you defeated your own Uruk war-leader.\n4\tTalk to Bregoleth at Idhobel\tBregoleth is at the camp of Idhobel, in Western Eregion.\n",
[1880]="700579FC\n1\tTalk to Merethien inside Merethrond, at a table on the east side of the hall, when you are ready to conclude the wedding-feast\tMerethien, the Master Foodmonger, can be found inside the great feast-hall of Merethrond, where the festivities continue.\n2\tTalk to Queen Arwen in the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\030Talk to King Elessar in the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tKing Elessar and Queen Arwen Undómiel have slipped away from the celebration and are in the throne room of Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n3\tTalk to Mithrandir outside the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tMithrandir is outside the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n",
[1881]="7003FDDB\n1\tThe entrance to Dol Amroth is west of the Cave of the Avorrim. Dorthaneth has asked you to bring what she knows of the Heirs of Castamir and the Umbar raiders to Lothíriel in Dol Amroth. You should first present yourself to the guards at the gate of the city.\t\n2\tTalk to a guard by the entrance to Dol Amroth\tThe entrance to Dol Amroth is west of the Cave of the Avorrim. Dorthaneth has asked you to bring what she knows of the Heirs of Castamir and the Umbar raiders to Lothíriel in Dol Amroth. You should first present yourself to the guards at the gate of the city.\n3\tFind Lothíriel in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth\tYou have presented yourself to the guards at the entrance to Dol Amroth and should now find Lothíriel in the Great Hall of the city.\n4\tTalk to Lothíriel in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth\tYou have presented yourself to the guards at the entrance to Dol Amroth and should now find Lothíriel in the Great Hall of the city.\n",
[1882]="7000013B\n1\tBring the lilies to Tom Bombadil\030Collect large lilies (total: 4)\tThe river flows westward from the house of Tom Bombadil. You found Tom Bombadil and spoke with the strange creature. While he was not at first willing to find the crebain he did at last relent, if you would perform a task he considered far more important. He wishes you to gather lilies from the river, near someone called Old Man Willow.\n",
[1883]="70061BD4\n1\tDefeat Uruks within Tham Celechir (total: 8)\030Search debris piles within Tham Celechir for notable artifacts\tTham Celechir is located on a hill to the north of Idhobel. Bregoleth wants to oppose the enemies that now hold Tham Celechir, the Hall of the Swift River.\n2\tBring the Elf-knife to Bregoleth at Idhobel\tBregoleth is waiting at Idhobel for news of your successful endeavours at Tham Celechir, the Hall of the Swift River.\n",
[1884]="7000A893\n1\tTalk to Laerdan\tLaerdan is in his room atop the stairs behind the door on your right as you enter keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Calenglad told you that Laerdan wishes to speak with you about the palantír and asked you to persuade him that the Dúnedain must win a decisive victory in Annúminas before it will be possible to reclaim the palantír.\n2\tTalk to Tadan\tRanger Tadan is on guard in the prison atop the stairs through the door on your left as you enter the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Laerdan has expressed his concern that Mordrambor is intentionally keeping you occupied in Annúminas while Amarthiel searches for Narchuil with the palantír.\n3\tTalk to Mordrambor\tMordrambor is in the prison atop the stairs through the door on your left as you enter the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Tadan has told you he will look forward to Laerdan's visit, because guarding Mordrambor is not pleasant, especially as the prisoner has begun reciting the various exploits of his brethren.\n",
[1885]="70034328\n1\tCollect dried herb bundles from Orcs in the High Knolls (total: 5)\tOrcs throughout the High Knolls may carry dried herb bundles. Nona has asked you to recover dried herb bundles the Orcs stole from Byre Tor to try and speed the recovery of the people in her care.\n2\tBring the dried herb bundles to Nona in her cave\tNona is in her cave in the High Knolls, and is waiting for you to return with the dried herb bundles you collected.\n3\tThrow dried herb bundles into the fire in the other chamber\tNona has asked you to throw the dried herb bundles you collected into the cooking fire in the cave chamber with the dying man. She hopes it will improve his condition.\n4\tTalk to the dying man\tThe smoke of the burning herbs has slightly revived the most injured of Nona's survivors.\n5\tTalk to Nona\030Talk to Horn\030Talk to Corudan\tYou have found the man you came into Wildermore to find, and should now tell your companions.\n6\tTalk to Gléowine\tGléowine is in Nona's cave, and wishes to speak with you.\n",
[1886]="7000A894\n1\tTalk to Tadan\tRanger Tadan is on guard in the prison atop the stairs behind the door on your left as you enter the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Mordrambor has told you of Tann Morgul, the artifact wielded by one of his brethren and says that its power can destroy the Dúnedain. Ranger Tadan is eager to speak with you about this new development.\n2\tCollect Tann Morgul\tGuldurchir is in Menelband, a courtyard located on the uppermost level of Annúminas. Ranger Tadan has told you where to find Guldurchir; he hopes you will be able to defeat this Black Númenórean before he is permitted to use the relic he carries, Tann Morgul, against the Dúnedain.\n3\tBring Tann Morgul to Mordrambor\tMordrambor is in the prison atop the stairs behind the door on your left as you enter the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. You have done what Mordrambor believed you could not: you defeated Guldurchir and wrested Tann Morgul from his clutches. You should bring the artifact now to Mordrambor to show that he was wrong.\n4\tBring Tann Morgul to Tadan\tRanger Tadan is in the prison atop the stairs through the door on your left as you enter the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Tadan has called you out of your reverie, preventing you from freeing Mordrambor and handing him Tann Morgul!\n",
[1887]="70034444\n1\tTalk to Elda\030Talk to Ymma\030Talk to Léodwig\030Talk to Elfgifu\tGléowine has determined that he can best help the survivors of Byre Tor by sending you to help them with their problems. He has asked you to speak to each of them and learn what it is they most want.\n2\tCollect stolen heirlooms from Orcs within Byre Tor (total: 6)\030Free horses from the stables of Byre Tor (total: 3)\030Defeat Foshnu or Krítar in Byre Tor\tOrcs in and around Byre Tor may possess stolen heirlooms for you to recover. The horses of Byre Tor can be found tied up at the stables near the top of the hill on which the city stands. Foshnu and Krítar will be somewhere within the city. You have learned what the survivors of the attack on Byre Tor under Nona's care desire of you, and now you should make certain you can accomplish what they want.\n3\tReturn the stolen heirlooms to Elda in Nona's cave\030Talk to Ymma\030Talk to Léodwig\030Talk to Elfgifu\tYou have done much good in Byre Tor, and should return to Nona's cave to tell the people in her care what you accomplished.\n4\tTalk to Gléowine\tGléowine is in Nona's cave in the High Knolls, and will be pleased to hear of your successful return to Byre Tor.\n5\tSpeak with Nona\tNona is in the other chamber of her cave in the High Knolls, and is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[1888]="7000A895\n1\tTalk to Laerdan\tLaerdan is in his room atop the stairs through the door on your right as you enter the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Tadan has told you that Laerdan believes he has learned the location of the palantír and knows how it can be reclaimed.\n2\tTalk to Golodir\tGolodir is in the Ranger-camp of Gath Forthnír, in East Angmar. Laerdan has sent you to speak with Golodir about acquiring some means with which to reclaim the palantír from Amarthiel.\n",
})
